{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 269,
    "dDurationMs": 4661,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's cut to the chase: How does the Higgs\nfield \"give\" particles mass? (and to be clear,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4930,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we're talking about the Higgs field and NOT\nthe Higgs Boson, which is merely an excitation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8590,
    "dDurationMs": 2529,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leftover after the process we're about to\nexplain."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11119,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I digress…back to mass!)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13219,
    "dDurationMs": 3811,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To begin, we need to know what we even mean\nby \"mass\" - so we'll head the other direction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17030,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and talk about what it means to be massless:\nThis may sound crazy, but the defining feature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20900,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of any particle without mass is that it travels\nat the speed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24050,
    "dDurationMs": 4090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, if we're honest it should really\nbe called the \"speed of massless particles,\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28140,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but since the first massless particles we\nknew about were photons of light, the name"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31770,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has stuck."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32770,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Anyway, the point is that all massless particles\ntravel 300 million meters every second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37370,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The details of this are explained by special\nrelativity, but simply put, it's physically"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41120,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "impossible for a massless particle to NOT\ntravel at 300 million meters per second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44870,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They can travel in a straight line or bounce\noff of things and change direction, but the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45870,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "speed of a massless particle never changes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46870,
    "dDurationMs": 2459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so mass is just the property of NOT HAVING\nTO always travel at the speed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49329,
    "dDurationMs": 4121,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a side effect, this also means not being\nABLE to travel at the speed of light, but"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53450,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the key is that particles with mass are lucky\nenough that they get to travel at ANY speed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56700,
    "dDurationMs": 2449,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they want – as long as it's slower than\nlight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59149,
    "dDurationMs": 3411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The amount of mass something has just tells\nhow hard it is for it to change from one of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62560,
    "dDurationMs": 1409,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these speeds to another."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63969,
    "dDurationMs": 3521,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, in Part I we mentioned that if there\nwere no Higgs field in the Standard Model,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67490,
    "dDurationMs": 2909,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ALL particles should be massless and thus\ntravel at the speed of light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70399,
    "dDurationMs": 3731,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But you and I and swiss cheese clearly have\nmass, because we have the beautiful luxury"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74130,
    "dDurationMs": 2089,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of being able to sit still."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76219,
    "dDurationMs": 1951,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how does the Higgs field help us do that?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78170,
    "dDurationMs": 4049,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, while massless particles can only travel\nat the speed of light, they ARE allowed to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82219,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bounce off of things."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83219,
    "dDurationMs": 4271,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Things like particles, which are really just\nexcitations in a quantum field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87490,
    "dDurationMs": 4629,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, the electron field is more concentrated\nat certain places called \"electrons\" - and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92119,
    "dDurationMs": 2230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "everywhere else is \"empty space\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94349,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the Higgs field is unusual in that it\nhas a high value EVERYWHERE – and to be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98219,
    "dDurationMs": 4481,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "clear, this high value is NOT the famous Higgs\nBoson - that's an extra excitation in addition"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102700,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to this already elevated field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104680,
    "dDurationMs": 4249,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But because the Higgs field has this everywhere\nnon-zero value, any particle that CAN interact"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108929,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with it is pretty much bouncing off of it\nall the time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111429,
    "dDurationMs": 4241,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if a massless particle bounces back and\nforth and back and forth (or, since it's quantum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115670,
    "dDurationMs": 4019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mechanics, does both at the same time), then\neven though in between bounces it travels"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119689,
    "dDurationMs": 3761,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the speed of light, when you add everything\nup it LOOKS like the particle is going slower"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123450,
    "dDurationMs": 1019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124469,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125469,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like it's not moving!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126469,
    "dDurationMs": 4111,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And since only things with mass are allowed\nto not move, our massless particle now looks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130580,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and acts like it has mass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132440,
    "dDurationMs": 1570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well done, Higgs!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134010,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What's more, the Higgs field can even interact\nwith its own excitations, which is to say,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137870,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it can give mass to the Higgs Boson, too."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140450,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Actually, the Higgs field likes to interact\nwith itself so much more than with the lowly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143890,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "electrons and protons that make us up, that\nthe Higgs Boson has a great deal more mass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147690,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "– and that's part of why it's been so hard\nto find."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148690,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But we shouldn't complain, because even though\nthe Higgs has given us a lot of trouble and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151490,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only a little bit of mass, at least we have\nmass, which allows us the simple pleasure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155570,
    "dDurationMs": 800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of not moving."
    } ]
  } ]
}
